.TH SDL_HINT_RENDER_LINE_METHOD 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_HINT_RENDER_LINE_METHOD \- A variable controlling how the 2D render API renders lines.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_hints.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_HINT_RENDER_LINE_METHOD \(dqSDL_RENDER_LINE_METHOD\(dq
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The variable can be set to the following values:
.PP

\(bu \(dq0\(dq: Use the default line drawing method (Bresenham\(aqs line algorithm)
.PP
\(bu \(dq1\(dq: Use the driver point API using Bresenham\(aqs line algorithm (correct, draws many points)
.PP
\(bu \(dq2\(dq: Use the driver line API (occasionally misses line endpoints based on hardware driver quirks
.PP
\(bu \(dq3\(dq: Use the driver geometry API (correct, draws thicker diagonal lines)
.PP
This hint should be set before creating a renderer\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This hint is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

